+Either form of the directory accepts a specialty filter, leaving only the veterinarians who hold the named specialty `[REQ-VET-004]`. The reader names the specialty in the request; neither form carries a control for picking one. A name matches a specialty in full and disregards letter case, so the opening letters of a specialty match nothing. Naming a specialty no veterinarian holds gives the ordinary directory with no veterinarian in it, rather than a failure. Naming nothing, or only spaces, gives the whole directory, as an empty owner search does. Paging through a filtered directory keeps the filter.
 
